WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.270
- When I watch this sequence, I love that

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:19.503
I still get emotional as he
becomes the fastest man alive.

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:22.260
- And one of the things
people don't realize

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.800
is that all the in-flight
dialogue was recorded in flight.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.420
You feel it in the movie.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.160
They're experiencing the G-forces.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:30.660
They're having trouble breathing.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.573
It puts you in the plane, it's amazing.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:37.800
- One thing about this one for us

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.610
was we got to not only
make a cool sounding car,

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:44.373
but also treat it almost like a beast.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.770
For the most part, what
you're hearing there

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:52.230
is actually a bottle
rocket just slowed down

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:56.130
from being one second long
to being 60 seconds long.

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:58.980
And then me on sampler just
kind of manipulating it

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:01.623
to give it the pitch rise
that I wanted it to have.

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:09.600
- Clarity is king, the whole
Way of Water is about a family,

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.580
it's about an emotional journey.

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:15.510
We were trying to make sure
that the story got told

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:18.783
in the most emotional and valuable way.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:24.720
- Baz wanted a whirlwind of sound

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:27.240
because at this point in
the film in the 1950s,

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:28.860
it was a frightening and dangerous time

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.080
for the establishment
because at this point,

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:34.203
Elvis Presley shifted the
cultural landscape of America.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:42.900
- We go to all the
extremes, light and dark,

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:47.850
loud and quiet, brutality
that doesn't hold back

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:50.760
to the delicate moments of devastation,

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:53.407
all the emotions that
the soldiers went through

00:01:53.407 --> 00:01:55.473
in the story and in the war.

